    {
      "key": "overlapping-hands-ready-stance",
      "name": {
        "en": "Overlapping Hands Ready Stance",
        "ko": "기본 준비자세",
        "romanized": "Gyeopson Junbijase"
      },
      "category": "stance",
      "video_timestamp": 164,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Gyeop-seon Jun-bi-ja-sae is a preparation posture in which both arms straighten from",
          "timestamp": 166.3,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mo-ha-seo-gi.",
          "timestamp": 171.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "The left hand is placed over the back of the right hand in the shape of a cross.",
          "timestamp": 173.3,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "The hands should be slightly apart from the body in front of the lower abdomen",
          "timestamp": 179.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the palm of the left hand placed over the back of the right hand in the",
          "timestamp": 184.7,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 197
    },
    {
      "key": "elbow-upward-strike",
      "name": {
        "en": "Elbow Upward Strike",
        "ko": "손날몸통바깥막기",
        "romanized": "Palggumchi Ollyeochigi"
      },
      "category": "strike",
      "video_timestamp": 197,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Par-gum-chi Oryeo-chigi is a technique to strike upward using the elbow.",
          "timestamp": 199.1,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "The basic target is an opponent's chin, but it can also be used to strike the solar",
          "timestamp": 209.4,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "plexus, chest, and other areas.",
          "timestamp": 214.7,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "When performing the move, make sufficient use of the twisting of your torso with",
          "timestamp": 218.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "your elbow close to your body.",
          "timestamp": 223.7,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 238
    },
    {
      "key": "augmented-high-side-block",
      "name": {
        "en": "Augmented High Side Block",
        "ko": "제비품안치기",
        "romanized": "Geodeureo Ulgul Yeopmakgi"
      },
      "category": "block",
      "video_timestamp": 238,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Go-do-ro-ol-gul-yeop-mak-gi",
          "timestamp": 238.6,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Starts with the Chagin-dol-jogui posture.",
          "timestamp": 241.8,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "The blocking arm should pass the face and the elbow and placed to your side",
          "timestamp": 246.7,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "level with your philtrum.",
          "timestamp": 251.1,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your elbow should straighten and be perpendicular to the ground.",
          "timestamp": 253.3,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 276
    },
    {
      "key": "pulling-backfist-front-strike",
      "name": {
        "en": "Pulling Back Fist Front Strike",
        "ko": "(몸통)안막기",
        "romanized": "Danggyeo Deungjumeok Apchigi"
      },
      "category": "strike",
      "video_timestamp": 276,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Dangyeo-deung-joo-mok-ap-chigi is a technique to pull an opponent with one",
          "timestamp": 278.1,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "hand and strike their face in the philtrum or chin forward from the inside",
          "timestamp": 282.5,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "using the other back fist.",
          "timestamp": 288.1,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "It can also be used to attack other areas depending on the situation.",
          "timestamp": 290.8,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "The back fist is placed in front of the philtrum.",
          "timestamp": 297.1,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 306
    },
    {
      "key": "yoke-strike",
      "name": {
        "en": "Yoke Strike",
        "ko": "올려(얼굴)막기",
        "romanized": "Meongyechigi"
      },
      "category": "strike",
      "video_timestamp": 306,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Mong-ae-chigi is a technique used to attack both sides using the elbow",
          "timestamp": 307.0,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "by crossing your arms above and below in front of the chest.",
          "timestamp": 315.0,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your back fist must face upward, and the back of your two hammer fists should",
          "timestamp": 320.3,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "lightly touch your chest.",
          "timestamp": 324.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your arms must be parallel.",
          "timestamp": 327.8,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 343
    },
    {
      "key": "spreading-mountain-block",
      "name": {
        "en": "Spreading Mountain Block",
        "ko": "학다리서기",
        "romanized": "Hecheo Santeulmakgi"
      },
      "category": "block",
      "video_timestamp": 343,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Hae-choo-san-teul-mak-i is a technique where your arms cross at the lower abdomen",
          "timestamp": 343.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "and move your sides horizontally in front of your face to perform ol-geul-hae-choo-mak-i",
          "timestamp": 351.4,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "with your inner wrist.",
          "timestamp": 357.0,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your arms should be at the philtrum level and perpendicular to the ground.",
          "timestamp": 359.9,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Be careful not to let the wrist bend and the blocking arm must not tilt front, back,",
          "timestamp": 366.4,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 375
    },
    {
      "key": "closed-stance",
      "name": {
        "en": "Closed Stance",
        "ko": "자전발",
        "romanized": "Moaseogi"
      },
      "category": "stance",
      "video_timestamp": 375,
      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Mo-ha-seo-gi is a posture where the back of the foot blades are adjacent to",
          "timestamp": 375.7,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "and the knees are straightened and aligned to the center line.",
          "timestamp": 380.6,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "Your eyes should be directed forward and be careful not to let space exist between your feet.",
          "timestamp": 385.4,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "These are the 7 key moves of pyeong-won-poom-se.",
          "timestamp": 392.2,
          "source": "caption"
        },
        {
          "text": "We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.",
          "timestamp": 398.3,
          "source": "caption"
        }
      ],
      "video_timestamp_end": 435
    },
